# Auto-commit Exp work

This workspace overrides “only commit when asked.” If this turn changed files, **commit before you finish talking.** Do not push. Do not promote.

## Where

| Edits in | Commit in | Branch |
|---|---|---|
| `F:\Mikes-UI-Exp` | that folder | `experimental` |
| `F:\Mikes-HALO-Jump-Exp` | that folder | `experimental` |
| `F:\Mikes-Invade-and-Annex-Exp` | that folder | `experimental` |

Never `git checkout experimental` in a production folder. Never commit `addon.gproj`. Skip `resourceDatabase.rdb`.

## How

Follow the git safety protocol: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log` (for style), stage only the files you changed, commit with a HEREDOC message, then `git status` to verify.

Message: 1–2 sentences on **why**, not a file list. Match that repo’s recent log style.

Skip the commit if there is nothing to commit. If several Exp repos changed, commit each separately.

Do not commit production addon scripts. Cursor rules, skills, and `tools\` under I&A may be committed in the folder you actually edited.
